The above solution is already implemented in our LockStealingDistributedLock
in our concurrent library.

The next improvement I can think of is to have priority for lock contenders in the turnstile.

For example when I try to steal the lock I will creep into his turnstile using a RPCish thread.
Good this thread needs to be given lower priority such that if there were two more local threads
behind me they should go ahead before I take the lock away. Of course come up with heuristics/magic
for the number 2 but you get my point.

As you can imagine moving a lock is the easy / cheap part but locks protect shared data moving that data
takes time. So if you can delay it a bit and get more throughput by all means.

